keywords:
  - El Niño–Southern Oscillation
  - heat-related mortality
  - heatwaves
  - drought
  - farmer suicides
  - foodgrain production
  - India
  - climate and health
abstract: >-
  State-level panels of NCRB-recorded heat/sun-stroke deaths (2001–2024), farming-sector
  suicides (2001–2023, aggregated state-year counts) and foodgrain production (1997–2016) in
  34 Indian units, compiled from official documents, with ENSO indices, IMD-based climate
  exposures, population denominators, the Python pipeline that builds them and the R analysis
  (negative binomial mixed models, leave-one-El-Niño-out and rolling-origin validation,
  mediation through heatwave days, temperature and monsoon onset, and 2027 projections) of the
  associated paper.
